Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their usage for this task  
• `event_date` : filter to the required calendar day (`'20210102'`).  
• `user_pseudo_id` : the anonymised user id – use it to isolate the single visitor (`'1402138.5184246691'`).  
• `event_name` : helps us keep only page‑view–type hits (normally `page_view`).  
• `event_params` : repeated record that actually contains the URL and title in the keys  
  – most frequently the keys are `page_location` (full URL), `page_path` (relative path), `page_title` (title).  
• `event_timestamp` : can be used for ordering the sequence of pages.  

Typical conditions  
‒ `event_date = '20210102'`  
‒ `user_pseudo_id = '1402138.5184246691'`  
‒ `event_name = 'page_view'` (optional when we only want page views)  

Below are ten progressively richer inspection queries (all limited to 20 rows) that lead up to the final answer.  
NB: only the table that contains 2‑Jan‑2021 data is referenced –  
`bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`.

```sql
-- 1) Get a feeling for the types of events this user generated on 2‑Jan‑2021
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
WHERE event_date = '20210102'
  AND user_pseudo_id = '1402138.5184246691'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Peek at the raw event_params array for a couple of rows
SELECT event_timestamp, event_params
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
WHERE event_date = '20210102'
  AND user_pseudo_id = '1402138.5184246691'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) All keys that appear inside event_params for this user on that day
SELECT DISTINCT ep.key
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102` AS t
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(t.event_params) AS ep
WHERE t.event_date = '20210102'
  AND t.user_pseudo_id = '1402138.5184246691'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Extract the page_location URL for every hit, without yet filtering on event_name
SELECT event_timestamp,
       ep.value.string_value AS page_location
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102` AS t
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(t.event_params) AS ep
WHERE t.event_date = '20210102'
  AND t.user_pseudo_id = '1402138.5184246691'
  AND ep.key = 'page_location'
ORDER BY event_timestamp
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Same for page_title
SELECT event_timestamp,
       ep.value.string_value AS page_title
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102` AS t
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(t.event_params) AS ep
WHERE t.event_date = '20210102'
  AND t.user_pseudo_id = '1402138.5184246691'
  AND ep.key = 'page_title'
ORDER BY event_timestamp
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Only page_view events and their URLs
SELECT DISTINCT ep.value.string_value AS page_location
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102` AS t
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(t.event_params) AS ep
WHERE t.event_date = '20210102'
  AND t.user_pseudo_id = '1402138.5184246691'
  AND t.event_name = 'page_view'
  AND ep.key = 'page_location'
